      "writtenOn": "2025-09-11T09:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are an awful lot of `#include \u003clinux/iio/types.h\u003e` so adding the macro after each one isn\u0027t really a good idea.\n\nYou could change from `ln` to `sed` in `tools/iio/Makefile`.\n\n```\nln -sf $(CURDIR)/../../include/uapi/linux/iio/types.h $@\n```\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\n/^enum iio_chan_type {/i\\\n#include \u003clinux/android_kabi.h\u003e\\\nANDROID_KABI_ENUMERATOR_IGNORE(iio_chan_type, IIO_ATTENTION);\\\n (there is a blank line here)\n```\n\n```\nsed -f iio.sed $(CURDIR)/../../include/uapi/linux/iio/types.h $@\n```\n\nYou\u0027d probably put the `sed` script inline in the `Makefile`. Just work out how many backslashes and quotes you need. :-)",
      "parentUuid": "2cd2b60b_54166166",
