      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e don\u0027t actually know what that ln is doing. It almost looks overwriting the internal one with the external one, but that cannot be right. Right?! (Please confirm.)\n\n`tools/iio` do the ln so the uapi is \"copied\" under `tools/iio/include/linux/iio/types.h` \n\n\nthat way, the compiler will use that file instead of `/usr/include/linux/iio/types.h` \n\n\n\n\u003e If the ln is a red herring, then all you should have to do is move the macro stuff to the internal types.h.\n\nThat will work. but the macro will be in a different location than the enum. If you are ok with that I can do the change.\n\nThanks!",
